{
 "version": 2,
 "doc": [
  "Shared test vectors for the retraction rule: the node (internal/store) and the dashboard read this same file.",
  "A retraction is an ordinary ack record. A message M is retracted iff the log holds an ack whose id is",
  "'retract:'+M.id or 'retract-leak:'+M.id and whose by is on the same machine as M.from (the machine is the",
  "text before the first '/', lower case; an identity without '/' is all machine). M.id is exactly ten",
  "lowercase hex digits. The effective retractor and time are the earliest such ack's (at, then by in byte",
  "order); leak is true if any such ack is a retract-leak. The ack's via and chars are ignored. Retraction",
  "is final, never expires, and applies in any arrival order, including before the message. Acks that follow",
  "the rule's id shape but are by another machine are 'ineffective' (counted, shown to an operator, change",
  "nothing). A retraction ack is not a read receipt: 'reads' lists every other ack, as (id, by), sorted.",
  "Each case: 'records' (replication records; per origin the seq are 1.. in order), 'expect.retracted'",
  "(message id -> the effective retractor, time and leak; absent = not retracted), 'expect.ineffective'",
  "(distinct (message id, by) claims for held messages by an identity not on the sender's machine, sorted by",
  "id then by) and 'expect.reads'. Implementations must give the same answer for every order in which the",
  "records of different origins are applied and after a restart that replays them. Ack ids containing",
  "control characters are not here on purpose: a replicating node stores such a record as a placeholder.",
  "version 2 adds cases for machine names that are not plain ASCII, which pin Go's behaviour so another",
  "implementation does the same: the machine name is lower-cased per rune with Go's strings.ToLower (simple",
  "case mapping, no full case folding, no special casing), compared whole, and identities that tie in time are",
  "ordered by UTF-8 bytes. It also adds 'tombstone_who': the table for msg.TombstoneWho, how a tombstone names",
  "a retractor: HostOf(by), then every rune outside [a-z0-9._-] becomes '?', then at most 40 runes (more than 40:",
  "the first 40 and '...'). A reader that does not know a top-level key must ignore it."
 ],
